## Artefact 4: ABC News Report (2024) – Ethical Concerns in AI Decision‑Making

### Summary  
This 2024 ABC News report discusses ethical concerns arising from AI systems used in government services, employment screening, and predictive analytics. The segment highlights issues such as fairness, transparency, and accountability, and includes interviews with ethicists and ICT professionals. It explains how different ethical theories—utilitarianism, Kantian ethics, and virtue ethics—can lead to different conclusions about the same AI system. The report also shows how ethical frameworks are being used to guide policy development and organisational decision‑making in Australia.

### Reflection  
I selected this artefact because it directly connects ethical theory to real‑world ICT challenges in Australia. The report helped me understand how different ethical frameworks can produce different evaluations of the same technology, reinforcing the importance of critical thinking. It also demonstrated how ethical theory is used in practice by policymakers and ICT professionals. This artefact is meaningful because it shows the relevance of ethical reasoning in everyday decision‑making and highlights the societal impact of ICT systems. It strengthened my ability to apply ethical theories to real situations, which is a key learning outcome of the unit.

